# MSS LivePulse — environment variable template (NAMES ONLY, no secret values)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in real values for local
# development. `.env` and `.env.*` are git-ignored (except this `.env.example`),
# so real secrets are never committed.
#
# Rules (see design.md → Deployment and Environment → Environment variables):
#  - Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser bundle, and only
#    non-secret values may ever be placed in them (Req 21.8).
#  - Variables marked "SERVER-SIDE ONLY" MUST NEVER be exposed to the browser or
#    referenced from client code. Set them in Supabase / Vercel server
#    environments only.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (VITE_-exposed, safe for the browser) — non-secret values only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite-exposed Supabase project URL.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Vite-exposed Supabase anon key (RLS-gated public client access, not a secret).
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared / config (frontend + server) — non-secret
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase project URL.
SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase anon key for RLS-gated client access.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Public base URL of the deployed SPA. Used by the create-event Edge Function to
# build the audience/presenter/QR URLs (Req 1.1). Falls back to the request
# origin, then a local-dev default, when unset. Non-secret.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# Comma-separated CORS allow-list of SPA origins permitted to call the Edge
# Functions. When unset (local dev), the request origin is echoed. Non-secret.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — NEVER expose to the browser / never bundle into client code
# (Set only in Supabase / Vercel server environments.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY: Service role key for Edge Function privileged writes (Req 21.8).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY: AEAD key for the credential encryption fallback;
# required only when the encryption fallback path is used (Req 12.5).
AI_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY: Deployment-level SSRF destination allowlist (Req 13.8).
AI_ENDPOINT_ALLOWLIST=
